Both accounts start with $\$2000$ at $10\%$ p.a. One pays simple interest and one compounds annually.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\definecolor{blue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{red}{HTML}{EF6068}
\definecolor{housegrid}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\begin{axis}[width=7cm,height=5.2cm,axis lines=left,axis line style={black,-{Stealth}},xmin=0,xmax=5.8,ymin=0,ymax=3700,xtick={0,1,2,3,4,5},ytick={0,1000,2000,3000},grid=both,grid style={color=housegrid,line width=0.25pt},clip=false,scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={color=black,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont,/pgf/number format/fixed},label style={color=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont},xlabel={Years},ylabel={Balance (\$)}]
\addplot[thick,blue,dashed,domain=0:5,samples=2]{2000+200*x};
\addplot[thick,red,domain=0:5,samples=60]{2000*exp(x*ln(1.1))};
\path (axis cs:5,3000) node[blue,below right,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont] {$A$};
\path (axis cs:5,3221.02) node[red,above right,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont] {$B$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Identify each account from the graph and describe its shape.
